WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.133
<v DANA>Ray, when we were setting up, you brought
up used blades left sitting out. Why do

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:06.480
<v DANA>those stick with you?

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.041
<v RAY>[thoughtful] Honestly, because a used
blade is a sharp, just like a needle. It

00:00:11.041 --> 00:00:12.640
<v RAY>just doesn't look like one.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.120
<v DANA>I always picture needles. So what counts
as a sharp?

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.983
<v RAY>A sharp is ANYTHING that can puncture or
cut the skin, so a used blade counts.

00:00:21.983 --> 00:00:27.054
<v RAY>Needles still show up too, because some
people manage diabetes or allergies with

00:00:27.054 --> 00:00:27.760
<v RAY>injections.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.680
<v DANA>Right. So how does a blade end up sitting
out?

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.826
<v RAY>Say you've just changed a blade, but the
sharps container is over by the other

00:00:35.826 --> 00:00:40.272
<v RAY>station. So you set the old one on top of
your toolbox and think, "I'll come right

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:41.040
<v RAY>back for it.".

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.921
<v DANA>[playful] That sounds kind of like
something I'd do. What's the harm if you

00:00:44.921 --> 00:00:45.760
<v DANA>come right back?

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.545
<v RAY>[matter-of-fact] Somebody else might
reach for that spot. A used blade is a

00:00:49.545 --> 00:00:52.000
<v RAY>hazard whether or not you can see
anything on it.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.320
<v DANA>Okay, back up. Say it's still in your
hand. What do you do?

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.532
<v RAY>You take it to the container. And
actually, you plan for this before you

00:01:00.532 --> 00:01:01.600
<v RAY>pick up the blade.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.640
<v DANA>How so?

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:08.146
<v RAY>There are four steps. One, know your
route to the container before you begin.

00:01:08.146 --> 00:01:14.014
<v RAY>Two, use a safer tool if one will do the
job. Three, turn on the safety feature if

00:01:14.014 --> 00:01:18.796
<v RAY>there is one. Four, put the blade
directly into a designated sharps

00:01:18.796 --> 00:01:19.520
<v RAY>container.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.680
<v DANA>It doesn't go on the toolbox. What about
the regular trash?

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.040
<v RAY>That's out too.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:28.800
<v RAY>A used blade goes STRAIGHT into the
container, every time.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:29.760
<v DANA>Got it.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.080
<v RAY>[warmly] What I tell crews: don't turn
that blade into somebody else's problem.

